  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Local Capacity of the Republic of Korea in Preparedness and Response to Natural and Man-Made Disasters</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Republic of Korea (ROK) plays a vital role in the peace and stability of the Asia Pacific region. It is one of the most heavily militarized countries in the world, as the country is technically still at war with its northern neighbor. The country&#x2019;s geographic location makes the country vulnerable to abrupt changes in power dynamics and various other geopolitical influences, while there have been persistent security threats due to the North. Further to the security threats, the country is exposed to greater risks of disasters due to climate change, which can exacerbate the impact of natural hazards. Extreme weather events have become more frequent than ever before in ROK, affecting the livelihoods of hundreds of thousands of people each year. 
 
The project aims to address persistent needs of ROK humanitarian actors in capacity development in emergency preparedness and response, by offering tailored trainings and knowledge support in most practical forms in addition to direct financial assistance for local non-government organizations to deliver Disaster Risk Reduction or emergency relief activities in case of a large-scale disaster in ROK.</narrative>
  </description>
